; OVERVIEW
; Bank 6, page 2 (8000H-BFFFH): the display, keyboard, RS-232C and timer IOCS, the
; arithmetic operators, character-code conversion, the 6x8 font and the built-in BASIC
; token table. Page 2 is switched to bank 6 by P0-B0 for every jump-table call that lands
; here (RST 18H 8000H-BFFFH) and by INTHND during interrupts.
; The jump table at 8000H-8122H is the target of the P0-B0 jump-table entries (T_<name>);
; the RST 18H entries at 8087H.. and 8117H.. forward to bank 3 (sound, LCD primitives).
; ============================================================================

; ---- I/O ports ----
P_LH10:     equ 10H     ; LH-5811 compatible block 10H-1FH (base)
